// D1629 — `__array_new__` filled with an INLINE ARRAY LITERAL. The fill is an element of the
// list being allocated, so it must build at the ELEMENT's list threading; left on the
// destination's it was built at the outer pair's heap types and the backing took the
// literal's own i32s.
//
// THE FILL MUST STAY AN INLINE LITERAL. Naming it first (`const s: i32[] = [0, 6]`) gives it
// a binding of its own and always ran, so a named-fill version of this template greens every
// cell for the wrong reason.
//
// The PROOF reads THROUGH the element (`v[1][1]`) at a non-zero member, so a row built at the
// wrong pair traps or prints the wrong number rather than passing.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@VALUE@@
__array_new__(2, [0, 6])
// @@TYPE@@
i32[][]
// @@PROOF@@
print(v[1][1])
// @@WANT@@
6
// @@VALUE2@@
__array_new__(2, [0, 8])
// @@TYPE2@@
i32[][]
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v[1][1] + 1)
// @@WANT2@@
9
